/* Resource id 1 (CREATEPROCESS_MANIFEST_RESOURCE_ID), type 24 (RT_MANIFEST).
   Spelled numerically so the script needs no Windows SDK headers, which the
   mingw cross-build does not have. */
1 24 "ShinraMeter-BPSR.manifest"

/* Resource id 2 (`platform::APP_ICON_RESOURCE_ID`). The `ICON` statement
   assigns this id to the auto-generated RT_GROUP_ICON (type 14) that groups
   the .ico's images; each individual image inside gets its own
   compiler-assigned RT_ICON (type 3) id. Explorer and the taskbar pick the
   group up automatically; `platform::tray_icon_handle` calls
   `LoadIconW(module, MAKEINTRESOURCE(2))`, which resolves against
   RT_GROUP_ICON, so id 2 must stay pinned to the `ICON` statement. */
2 ICON "assets/shinra.ico"
